{"kind":"request","text":"Please review the corrected J1 design note at the exact head, under request 7d6ce0f6 and promise 3649cf4a. It answers your report c4e862e6, so please read the diff from 40256d33. As before, this head holds only the note, and it will not land alone. Nothing has run.\n\nYour six items:\n1. Section 2 now says that no role reads a copy directly, and that a holder of membership.invite or the recovery key can reach one by adding a key to that member, which the journal shows.\n2. The seven days use the object's alarm. Wakes.set takes the minimum of its causes (outbox.ts:79-87), and membership already shares that alarm with key-invitation-end. Reading only; it has not run.\n3. Another key shows the open copy as having no answer yet, with the button, and keeps its acts. The lock follows the key that signed. A second tab in one browser holds the same key, so it follows the lock. The page's fence lives in memory, so the note locks on that fence or on an open row whose intent.actor is this page's key. There is a new case.\n4. The note names what a session gains and who holds one, and section 4 has a row for a stolen session. It recommends keeping holder(reader, \"summary\") and adding no ReadName. The reasons: readsOf gives every member the same list, so a new name narrows nothing, and isClaims refuses unknown names, so new tokens would fail every read at objects on old code during turnover or rollback. McpAgent holds an agent's seed, so its session names the agent and the member compare fails. A later head that gives a hosted server a person's session adds the name then. Please weigh this hardest.\n5. Section 5 states the second device's clock.\n6. A POST repeat with the same bytes returns 204 and charges nothing. Other bytes return 409 and keep the first. There is a new case. The routes answer only on an active membership scope.\n\nAlso carried: the landing's evidence measures the two added requests, section 9 states the turnover cost, and device-key